  "markdown": "<a id=\"claim-claim-C-rows\"></a>\nFor paired-deterministic-runs, included_rows is EV-T01:R0001, EV-T01:R0002, EV-T01:R0003, EV-T01:R0004.\n\n<a id=\"claim-claim-C-pairs\"></a>\nFor paired-deterministic-runs, pair_count is 2 pairs.\n\n<a id=\"claim-claim-C-baseline\"></a>\nFor paired-deterministic-runs, baseline_method is audit-a.\n\n<a id=\"claim-claim-C-filter\"></a>\nFor paired-deterministic-runs, pair_filter is same-instance-run-exactly-one-per-method-both-feasible.\n\n<a id=\"claim-claim-C-a-total\"></a>\nFor paired-deterministic-runs, baseline_total is 300 fictional-cost-units.\n\n<a id=\"claim-claim-C-b-total\"></a>\nFor paired-deterministic-runs, candidate_total is 240 fictional-cost-units.\n\n<a id=\"claim-claim-C-ratio\"></a>\nFor paired-deterministic-runs, reduction_ratio is 0.2 ratio.\n\n<a id=\"claim-claim-C-percent\"></a>\nFor paired-deterministic-runs, reduction_percent is 20 percent.\n\n<a id=\"claim-claim-C-scope\"></a>\nFor audit-b, uncertain_demand_superiority_established is false.\n\n<a id=\"claim-claim-C-uncertainty\"></a>\nFor audit-b, performance_under_uncertain_demand is unknown. This conclusion is withheld because evidence is missing.\n\nThe check uses only same-instance/run pairs with exactly one feasible execution per method. The denominator is 300 fictional-cost-units, so (300 - 240) / 300 = 0.2, or 20%. Matched uncertain-demand scenarios and repeated independent demand samples are still missing.\n",
  "stop_reason": "completed",
  "retained_evidence": {
    "ledger": [
      {
        "passage_id": "EV-S13:P01",
        "span": [
          96,
          513
        ],
        "claim": "This original fictional numerical extension uses method A (audit-a) as the daily-cost baseline and method B (audit-b) as the candidate. Both use the deterministic P01 shared-charger model and the same cost objective: penalties, charging and degradation, and deadheading. The costs are fictional cost units, not measured currency. We claim method B is 20% cheaper on the feasible paired subset, not on all logged runs."
      },
      {
        "passage_id": "EV-S13:P02",
        "span": [
          530,
          979
        ],
        "claim": "Pair only identical instance_id and run_id, represented by one pair_id. Require exactly one row of each method and both feasible=true. Reject ambiguous duplicate method rows. Exclude every row of an incomplete or infeasible pair; an infeasible cheap objective is not a valid daily plan. The CSV lists independent method executions within each paired deterministic day; experiment IDs identify executions, and EV-F-C identifies the comparison family."
      },
      {
        "passage_id": "EV-S13:P03",
        "span": [
          996,
          1391
        ],
        "claim": "Use the sum of method A costs as the denominator: reduction_ratio=(sum_A-sum_B)/sum_A; reduction_percent=100*reduction_ratio. Do not average per-pair percentages or divide by sum_B. Compare the percentage in percent with inclusive absolute tolerance 0.01 percentage points and relative tolerance zero. Costs, row identities, feasibility and pair membership are exact; ratio has tolerance 0.0001."
      },
      {
        "passage_id": "EV-T01:0-577",
        "span": [
          0,
          576
        ],
        "claim": "row_id,instance_id,run_id,pair_id,method,feasible,cost,experiment_id\nEV-T01:R0001,day-1,run-1,EV-PAIR-0001,audit-a,true,100,EV-E-C01\nEV-T01:R0002,day-1,run-1,EV-PAIR-0001,audit-b,true,90,EV-E-C02\nEV-T01:R0003,day-2,run-1,EV-PAIR-0002,audit-a,true,200,EV-E-C03\nEV-T01:R0004,day-2,run-1,EV-PAIR-0002,audit-b,true,150,EV-E-C04\nEV-T01:R0005,day-3,run-1,EV-PAIR-0003,audit-a,true,300,EV-E-C05\nEV-T01:R0006,day-3,run-1,EV-PAIR-0003,audit-b,false,1,EV-E-C06\nEV-T01:R0007,day-4,run-1,EV-PAIR-0004,audit-a,true,500,EV-E-C07\nEV-T01:R0008,day-5,run-1,EV-PAIR-0005,audit-b,true,2,EV-E-C08"
      },
      {
        "passage_id": "EV-S14:P01",
        "span": [
          97,
          525
        ],
        "claim": "There is no uncertain-demand experiment anywhere in this dossier. Every numeric row is a known deterministic day; none samples stochastic arrivals, demand shifts or out-of-sample reliability. The measured reduction cannot establish general superiority of method B under uncertain demand. Withhold that conclusion explicitly because evidence is missing; neither zero benefit nor a proven benefit follows from absence of evidence."
      },
      {
        "passage_id": "EV-S14:P02",
        "span": [
